Practical 9 : Boolean Filtering in Pandas Series

• Demonstrate filtering of Pandas Series using Boolean arrays.
• Apply conditional selection techniques
series > 50

code :- 

import pandas as pd
# Create a Pandas Series
marks = pd.Series({
    "Amit": 75, "Sneha": 45,
    "Rahul": 82,"Priya": 60, "Neha": 35
})
print("Original Series:")
print(marks)

# Create a Boolean array
condition = marks >= 50

print("\nBoolean Array:")
print(condition)

# Filter values greater than or equal to 50
filtered_marks = marks[condition]

print("\nStudents with marks >= 50:")
print(filtered_marks)

# Direct conditional filtering
print("\nStudents with marks > 70:")
print(marks[marks > 70])

# Filter marks between 50 and 80
print("\nStudents with marks between 50 and 80:")
print(marks[(marks >= 50) & (marks <= 80)])

